// How many machines come, tuned while the game runs.
//
// The game reads this file again whenever it is saved (BIMS_SCALING names
// another). The next wave laid and the next station's wave count take the
// new numbers; a wave already standing keeps its size. A field left out is
// the built-in value, and a file that does not parse keeps the last good
// numbers (the reason is printed on the terminal).
//
//   a wave            = base + per_player * players + per_step * steps
//   steps             = whole step_days of the world clock (a jump is a day)
//   waves at a site   = tier_waves by the tier its machines come at:
//                       (tier one, tier two, tier three)
//   the run's first mission: every wave first_mission_ease fewer, never under 1
//   the run's first early_days days (by the world clock): every wave early_ease
//                       fewer as well, never under 1
//
// Only player Bims count as players; bots do not.
//
// The game setup's Difficulty shows base, per_player and per_step (its
// "Scaling") as this file has them; once the host moves one, the run keeps
// the setup's three (saved with it, dealt to every guest) and this file
// still says the rest. The setup's "Save as default" writes its three
// numbers into this file, leaving the comments and the other lines alone.
// The built-in values: base 2, per_player 1, per_step 1, step_days 5,
// tier_waves (1, 2, 4), first_mission_ease 1, early_ease 0, early_days 6.
(
    base: 1,
    per_player: 1,
    per_step: 1,
    step_days: 5,
    tier_waves: (1, 2, 4),
    first_mission_ease: 1,
    early_ease: 5,
    early_days: 6,
)
